# Content & SEO

See also `docs/architecture.md` (registry + SEO helper).

## Never

- `git commit` / `git push` / amend / stage-and-commit (leave changes uncommitted; Paul commits)
- Email addresses or `mailto:` links
- A contact page or “Contact” nav/footer links
- Privacy/About links outside the **footer**
- “Report a map issue” anywhere
- “© OpenStreetMap contributors” in the footer (map attribution only)
- The words “Telemetry Extractor” / “telemetry extractor” as product naming
- The name **FlySight** (say “GNSS logger CSV exports”)
- Branding the product as GoPro or DJI (compatibility wording only)

## Allowed brand-in-URL exception

- `/gopro-gps-extract` only — copy must still differ from FlySync (privacy / multi-tool hub angle)
- Optional 301 from legacy `/gopro` → `/gopro-gps-extract`

## Every public page

- Unique title (≤ ~60 chars where possible) + meta description
- Canonical URL from env-aware `base_url`
- Add the route to `config/tools.php` (`inSitemap`); `/sitemap.xml` is generated, never hand-edited
- Privacy / About in footer only; no Contact

## `/gopro-gps-extract` pre-upload

- Drop zone first; rich original content below (intro, how-it-works, what you get including Video view, supported HERO GPS cameras as compatibility, privacy, FAQ, links to `/gpx-editor` / `/convert/...` + guides; map uses generic viewer module)
- Hide content block after a video loads
- Primary KW: `gopro gps extractor` (see `docs/seo-keywords.md`)

## Format landings (SEO pages, not the viewer)

- `/gpx-viewer`, `/kml-viewer`, `/kmz-viewer`, `/fit-viewer`, `/gopro-gps-extract` — each is an **SEO landing** (H1, intro, how-to, FAQ + drop zone)
- Landings run the matching parser, then hand the **track model** to the **generic viewer module** (`assets/js/viewer/`). View-only (GoPro also has a video view). Edit CTAs → `/gpx-editor`
- Link the matching format guide and `/convert/<pair>` / `/gpx-editor` where useful

## Editor + converter landings (same split)

- `/gpx-editor` and `/convert` + `/convert/<pair>` are **SEO landings** (content + drop zone → parse → hand track to `assets/js/editor/` or `assets/js/converter/`)
- Editor shares map/chart components with the viewer module

## Converter pages

- Hub: `/convert` · SEO pairs: `/convert/kml-to-gpx`, `/convert/gpx-to-kml`, `/convert/fit-to-gpx`, `/convert/kmz-to-gpx`, `/convert/gpx-to-kmz`, `/convert/kmz-to-kml`
- Each pair: short **unique** intro + FAQ · **self-canonical**
- Guides and footer links for important pairs point at `/convert/<pair>` (never the old `/kml-to-gpx` paths)

## Guides (`/guides/`)

- **Brief:** `docs/guides-brief.md` — Wave A/B slugs, angles, H2 outlines, internal links, keyword labels
- Prefer how-to / compare over pure definitions; distinct angle per page; cross-link instead of repeating definitions
- **Link targets:** converters → `/convert/<pair>` · open/view → format landings (`/gpx-viewer` …) · edit → `/gpx-editor`
- Link tools ↔ guides both ways
- Never invent Planner volumes; follow verified vs unverified labels in the brief
